1. The code currently checks for prime numbers by iterating from 2 to the number itself. However, this is not necessary. We only need to check up to the square root of the number to determine if it is prime.

2. The code does not handle the case when there are no prime numbers in the list. In this case, the function should return None, as it currently does. However, the print statement should be modified to handle this case as well.

